 "result_text": "Topic nodes no longer send the structured metadata fields, so Studio's \"must pass a list of values\" check shouldn't trip on them. I haven't run the tests or tried an upload against Studio. I only checked that `ricecooker.classes.nodes` still imports.\n\nBoth changes are in `ricecooker/classes/nodes.py`:\n- **`TreeNode.to_dict()`:** it no longer includes `grade_levels`, `resource_types`, `learning_activities`, `accessibility_categories`, `subjects` or `needs`. Topic nodes don't have these attributes, so they were always sent as `null`.\n- **`ContentNode.to_dict()`:** it now leaves out any of those six fields that are `None`. The issue only showed topic nodes failing, but a video or document node with, say, no `grade_levels` set would have sent `null` and hit the same Studio error.\n\nThe catch is that content nodes now omit unset fields instead of sending `null`. If anything downstream, including tests, expects those keys to always be present, it will need updating.",
